# Valgrind suppressions for poc's conservative garbage collector: pofltk's
# test/poc-gc.supp (from polibfyaml's) and ova_fmt_po's, in one file.
#
# GarbageCollectedHeap.Collect scans every word of the machine stack for
# things that look like heap pointers (poc's rtl/llvm/GarbageCollectedHeap.Mod),
# including words that were never written. Memcheck reports each such read
# as an uninitialised-value error with MarkCandidate as the top frame
# (polibfyaml, confirmed 2026-10-03); and in programs with bigger frames,
# such a word that happens to point into a block is traced from by
# DrainMarkStack (ova_fmt_po, confirmed 2026-10-09: 37 such errors from
# `ova_fmt_po -H`, nothing else). That is how a conservative collector
# works, not a bug in the program.
#
# Only uninitialised-value errors whose TOP frame is one of those two
# functions are suppressed; the same kinds of error anywhere else, and
# every invalid read or write and leak, are still reported.

{
   poc-gc-markcandidate-cond
   Memcheck:Cond
   fun:GarbageCollectedHeap.MarkCandidate
}
{
   poc-gc-markcandidate-value8
   Memcheck:Value8
   fun:GarbageCollectedHeap.MarkCandidate
}
{
   poc-gc-drainmarkstack-value8
   Memcheck:Value8
   fun:GarbageCollectedHeap.DrainMarkStack
}
